Z||000007||yo_sweet||08-16-2001||01:24 AM||||were delorens fast? what are there 0-60 like?<BR>how much hp? ??||||reg||1
Z||000008||sloth85GT||08-16-2001||01:26 AM||||They weren't fast at all. They had a weak 4 cylinder engine. Just look it up on the net, it'll be around somewhere cause I'm not sure.||||reg||1
Z||000009||The Fieromaster||08-16-2001||02:23 AM||||I beg to differ on the slow thing.. ther is a guy around here who has one.. its cool.. I sat in it and all... felt like it was missing somthing... OH YEA the flux capacitor!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> hehe!  Anyway it had a 2.8L and wasnt slow!  It wasnt FAST but it was quick...  For a 4,000lb beast it was quick!||||reg||10
Z||000010||EdsB52||08-16-2001||02:24 AM||||I think they had a Renault engine. So yes, it did suck.||||reg||1
Z||000011||sloth85GT||08-16-2001||04:57 AM||||didn't the Delorean come with a cheap ass I-4, I'm gonna chek on that one right now.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||sloth85GT||08-16-2001||05:22 AM||||Okay here's the scoop, not an I-4, never was an I-4. <P>-It was powered by an aluminum fuel injected 2.8L Peugot-Renault-Volvo V6 that had an output of 130HP. <BR>-0-60 in almost 8 seconds<BR>-Only 8583 Deloreans were manufactured from 81 to 83<BR>-3 gold plated versions were built as well<BR>-The Delorean weighed 2712 pounds<BR>-height is 45" (one inch lower than a Fiero)<BR>-body panels were unpainted stainless steel<P>The more and more I learn about the Delorean, the more it seems to resemble my beloved Fiero!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">  <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT<P>WITH THE NEW WHEELS!!!!! WOOHOO!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000013||btoth||08-16-2001||10:50 AM||||Thanks for the facts.  I knew it was pretty close in stats to the Fieros.  Just more exotic.  Maybe now we'll stop hearing about how "slow" and "heavy"they are. <P><BR>Edit:<P>And you can get a performance 2.8 from DMC in Texas.  You can also get your DeLorean completely refurbished for the right amount of money. Or you can just buy a completely refurbished DeLorean from them for $20k.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.delorean.com" TARGET=_blank>www.delorean.com</A> <P><BR>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 08-16-2001).]<BR> <A HREF="http://www.delorean.com/english/Performance/performance.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.delorean.com/english/Performance/performance.asp</A> <p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 08-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Cheever3000||08-16-2001||11:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Or you can just buy a completely refurbished DeLorean from them for $20k.<BR><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Actually it's $29,500.  See the "sales" link in the URL you posted...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.delorean.com/english/Sales/sales.asp" TARGET=_blank>http://www.delorean.com/english/Sales/sales.asp</A> <P>||||reg||1
