Z||000045||Ken Wittlief||08-20-2001||09:52 AM||||The saddest part of the whole delorean story is that John wanted to make a car that would last 20 years or more - he was tired of detroits trend of making cars that rust away by design and end up in scrap yards.<P> so he figured using stainless and plastics he could build a frame and body that would be stylish for decades, and he designed the drivetrain to be replaceable - so you really could have a car that would last you 20 years or more, and that could rack up a million miles on the odo.<P>  He simply didnt have the backing to pull it off sucessfully - was a great idea though!||||reg||11
